  "footnotes": [
    {
      "marker": "a",
      "text": "If not already signed the ICF during the Run-in Period",
      "appears_complete": true,
      "attaches_to": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "b",
      "text": "Including mucosal biopsies. During screening, diagnostic colonoscopy or flexible sigmoidoscopy, at the discretion of the Investigator (if no diagnostic colonoscopy with serial biopsy has been performed within one year of screening, a full colonoscopy is required, to exclude malignancy), centrally read. Endoscopy conducted within 35 days before Randomisation is acceptable. At Visit 8, flexible sigmoidoscopy, centrally read.",
      "appears_complete": true,
      "attaches_to": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "c",
      "text": "The screening endoscopy should be performed at Day -35 to Day -6 prior to Randomisation.",
      "appears_complete": true,
      "attaches_to": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "d",
      "text": "The scores for stool frequency and rectal bleeding will be calculated as an average based on scores collected from the Patient daily Diary, for up to 5, but at least 3 days prior to each applicable visit. If the patient undergoes bowel preparation for endoscopy on any of the days before a visit, the stool frequency and rectal bleeding subscore for that day(s) should be considered missing. In addition, the stool frequency and rectal bleeding subscore will be considered missing for the day of all endoscopies and the day after.",
      "appears_complete": true,
      "attaches_to": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "e",
      "text": "For Mainland China PK subgroup only. At 1st dose: pre-dose and 0.5, 1, 2 (end of infusion), 6, 48, 144 (Day 6), and 240 (Day 10) h after the start of the 1st administration; At the 2nd, 3rd, 4th, and 5th administrations blood samples will be collected pre-dose and at the end of infusion; At 6th dose: pre-dose and 0.5, 1, 2 (end of infusion), 6, 48, 144 (Day 70), 240 (Day 80), 336 (Day 84), 480 (Day 90), and 840 h (Day 105) after the start of the 6th administration.",
      "appears_complete": true,
      "attaches_to": []
    },
    {
      "marker": "f",
      "text": "Biomarkers erythrocyte sedimentation rate [ESR], C-reactive protein (CRP), neutrophil and platelet count tests will be analysed in local sites. IL-6, IL-6/sIL-6R complex, and faecal calprotectin tests will be analysed in central lab. At Visits 2 and 8, the patient should be in a fasting state ( ≥8 hours).",
      "appears_complete": true,
      "attaches_to": [
        {
          "kind": "row",
          "row": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "marker": "g",
      "text": "Includes haematology, clinical chemistry, coagulation tests, and urinalysis assessments. Clinical laboratory test should be conducted -5 to -1 days prior to Randomisation.",
      "appears_complete": true,
      "attaches_to": [
        {
          "kind": "row",
          "row": 2
        }
      ]
    }
